{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1459, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given a positive integer N and two strings S and T, each of length N and consisting of lowercase English letters.\nFind the Hamming distance between S and T. That is, find the number of integers i such that 1 \\leq i \\leq N and the i-th character of S is different from the i-th character of T.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\r\nS\r\nT\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1\\leq N \\leq 100\n- N is an integer.\n- Each of S and T is a string of length N consisting of lowercase English letters.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n6\r\nabcarc\r\nagcahc\n\nSample Output 1\n\n2\r\n\nS and T differ in the 2nd and 5th characters, but not in other characters. Thus, the answer is 2.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n7\r\natcoder\r\ncontest\n\nSample Output 2\n\n7\n\nSample Input 3\n\n8\r\nchokudai\r\nchokudai\n\nSample Output 3\n\n0\n\nSample Input 4\n\n10\r\nvexknuampx\r\nvzxikuamlx\n\nSample Output 4\n\n4\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1503, "char_start": 1471, "quote": "Input:\n6\nabcarc\nagcahc\nOutput:\n2", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1549, "char_start": 1515, "quote": "Input:\n7\natcoder\ncontest\nOutput:\n7", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1597, "char_start": 1561, "quote": "Input:\n8\nchokudai\nchokudai\nOutput:\n0", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R6", "source": {"char_end": 1650, "char_start": 1609, "quote": "Input:\n10\nvexknuampx\nvzxikuamlx\nOutput:\n4", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 4: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "e82b2ab522a5001910b8d9bd70923307ac1e9f08cfaade754eaa55a851db611a", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "bc8489a15fa4bee41b2339c2284d7acc7e850ff3b67743a004f97a5f7bd9ec2d", "seq": 2}
